      "filename": "Alphonse de Neuville - The defence of Rorke's Drift 1879 - Google Art Project.jpg",
      "title": "File:Alphonse de Neuville - The defence of Rorke's Drift 1879 - Google Art Project.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/20/Alphonse_de_Neuville_-_The_defence_of_Rorke%27s_Drift_1879_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alphonse_de_Neuville_-_The_defence_of_Rorke%27s_Drift_1879_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg",
      "width": 5001,
      "height": 2967,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Alphonse de Neuville",
      "credit": "5AFi-BKNCeU_VA at Google Cultural Institute maximum zoom level",
      "source": "The defence of Rorke's Drift 1879title QS:P1476,en:\"The defence of Rorke's Drift 1879\"label QS:Len,\"The defence of Rorke's Drift 1879\"",
      "description": "Painting of the Battle of Rorke's Drift which took place in Natal during the Anglo-Zulu War in 1879. De Neuville based the painting on eye witness accounts and it depicts several events of the battle occurring at once. Defenders depicted in the painting:\nLieutenant John Chard (to the right at the barrier in pale breeches with rifle)\nCorporal Scammell of the Natal Native Contingent incorrectly shown in the uniform of the 24th or Corporal William Allen (handing cartridges to Chard)\nCorporal Ferdinand Schiess (wearing a bandoleer and stabbing a Zulu at the barrier with his bayonet)\nChaplain George Smith (bearded man handing out cartridges from a haversack)\nActing Assistant Commissary James Dalton (sat in foreground with a wounded shoulder)\nSurgeon James Reynolds (attending to Dalton's wound)\nLieutenant Gonville Bromhead (standing in the centre of the painting pointing to his left)\nPrivate Frederick Hitch (standing behind Bromhead)\nPrivate Henry Hook (carrying Private John Connolly on his back away from the burning hospital)\nAssistant Commissary Walter Dunne (to the left holding a biscuit box)\n(Sources: David, Saul [2005] Zulu: The Heroism and Tragedy of the Zulu War of 1879 ISBN 9780141015699; Knight, Ian [1996] Rorke's Drift 1879: 'Pinned Like Rats in a Hole' ISBN 9781855325067)",
      "dateCreated": "1880<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P571,+1880-00-00T00:00:00Z/9</div>",
      "sourceType": "core",
